---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContentSection from '../components/ContentSection.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';

// Sections are placed explicitly rather than looped, because the bespoke
// "problem", "partners" and "contact" blocks are interleaved between them.
const who = (await getEntry('sections', 'who'))!;
const offering = (await getEntry('sections', 'offering'))!;
const why = (await getEntry('sections', 'why'))!;
const how = (await getEntry('sections', 'how'))!;
const notDifferent = (await getEntry('sections', 'not'))!;
const investors = (await getEntry('sections', 'investors'))!;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Engine Factory: The commercial engine for deep-tech companies"
  description="Pipeline, pricing, customer contracts, and the team to run it. We de-risk commercial execution and compress the time between funding and first revenue for semiconductor and deep-tech companies."
>
  <div class="dark-wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <h1>The commercial engine for <em>deep-tech</em> companies.</h1>
        <hr class="rule">
        <p class="hero-lede">Pipeline, pricing, customer contracts, and the team to run it. We de-risk commercial execution and compress the time between funding and first revenue.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <main>
    <div class="container">

      <section id="problem">
        <span class="eyebrow">The challenge</span>
        <h2>Brilliant technology does not <em>sell itself</em>.</h2>
        <p>We hear the same conversations every week:</p>
        <div class="quotes">
          <blockquote>"We raised €8M, we have a working chip, and no idea how to sell it."</blockquote>
          <blockquote>"Our investors are asking about pipeline and we don't even have a CRM."</blockquote>
          <blockquote>"We hired a sales guy from a large semiconductor company. Six months in, nothing closed. He is used to inheriting a $200M installed base, not building from zero."</blockquote>
        </div>
        <p>The pattern is the same every time. The R&amp;D worked. The funding came through. But nobody in the building has ever priced a semiconductor, structured a distribution agreement, or closed a production contract with a Tier 1 customer.</p>
        <p>Every month without a commercial function is runway burned with no pipeline to show for it. Competitors are locking in design wins. The window between <em>funded</em> and <em>too late</em> is shorter than most founders think.</p>
      </section>

      <ContentSection section={who} />

      <ContentSection section={offering} />

      <section id="partners" class="oxblood-panel">
        <div class="panel-inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Partners</span>
          <h2>A <em>network</em> of senior operators.</h2>
          <p>The Engine Factory is built as a network of senior semiconductor commercial operators, each independent, each bringing deep expertise in a specific market, domain, or geography. A partner in Munich working on a European market entry. A partner in Detroit who knows the automotive Tier 1 landscape. A partner in Silicon Valley close to the venture ecosystem. When a client needs capability beyond one partner, the network delivers it.</p>
          <p>We are in the founding phase. New partners are joining in 2026. If you are a senior commercial operator in semiconductor or deep-tech and want to know more about joining, <a href="#contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
          <p class="bio-link" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/partners/">Meet the team →</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <ContentSection section={why} />

      <ContentSection section={how} />

      <ContentSection section={notDifferent} />

      <ContentSection section={investors} />

    </div>
  </main>

  <section id="contact">
    <div class="contact-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
      <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
      <p>We work with semiconductor and deep-tech companies that are past the R&amp;D phase and ready to build a commercial engine. If that sounds like you, or if you want to know more about joining the partner network, reach out.</p>

      <p class="contact-cta"><a href="https://zeeg.me/etiennewinkelmullerzeeg/introcall" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book an appointment</a></p>

      <div class="contact-grid">
        <div class="contact-block">
          <span class="label">Direct</span>
          <div class="name">Etienne Winkelmuller</div>
          <div class="name-sub">Founder</div>
          <address>
            <a href="mailto:etnw.mywebsite@pm.me">etnw.mywebsite@pm.me</a><br>
            <a href="tel:+498955273295">+49 89 55273295</a><br>
            <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/etiennewinkelmuller" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          </address>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-block">
          <span class="label">Office</span>
          <address>
            Sendlinger Strasse 29<br>
            80331 Munich<br>
            Germany
          </address>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
